{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788226636773,"sessionID":"ses_fa566fb65ffeJ8k4Q5FXGIEPJE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_91ddea790e4340c78607bf0e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\n\n# Seasons per file\ndef seasons(path, col, enc='utf-8'):\n    with open(path, newline='', encoding=enc) as f:\n        vals = Counter(r[col].strip() for r in csv.DictReader(f) if r.get(col))\n    return sorted(vals)\n\nprint(\"Brasileirao seasons:\", seasons('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv','season')[:3], \"...\", seasons('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv','season')[-3:])\nprint(\"Cup seasons:\", seasons('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv','season')[:3], \"...\", seasons('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv','season')[-3:])\nprint(\"Lib seasons:\", seasons('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv','season')[:3], \"...\", seasons('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv','season')[-3:])\nprint(\"Novo years:\", seasons('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv','Ano')[:3], \"...\", seasons('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv','Ano')[-3:])\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    years = Counter(r['date'][:4] for r in csv.DictReader(f) if r.get('date'))\nprint(\"BR years:\", sorted(years))\n\n# FIFA clubs w/ Brazil\nwith open('data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    clubs = Counter(); nats = Counter(); vals=set()\n    rows=0\n    for row in r:\n        rows+=1\n        if row['Nationality']=='Brazil': clubs[row['Club']]+=1\n        vals.add(row['Value'])\nprint(\"\\nFIFA rows:\", rows)\nprint(\"Brazilian players by club (top 20):\", clubs.most_common(20))\nprint(\"Value samples:\", sorted(vals)[:5], sorted(vals)[-3:])\nEOF"},"output":"Brasileirao seasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014'] ... ['2020', '2021', '2022']\nCup seasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014'] ... ['2019', '2020', '2021']\nLib seasons: ['2013', '2014', '2015'] ... ['2021', '2022', 'NA']\nNovo years: ['2003', '2004', '2005'] ... ['2017', '2018', '2019']\nBR years: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\n\nFIFA rows: 18207\nBrazilian players by club (top 20): [('Grêmio', 20), ('Atlético Mineiro', 20), ('Cruzeiro', 20), ('Fluminense', 20), ('Santos', 20), ('Internacional', 20), ('América FC (Minas Gerais)', 20), ('Botafogo', 20), ('Bahia', 20), ('Paraná', 20), ('Atlético Paranaense', 20), ('Vitória', 20), ('Sport Club do Recife', 20), ('Chapecoense', 20), ('Ceará Sporting Club', 20), ('Portimonense SC', 18), ('SC Braga', 13), ('CD Aves', 12), ('Rio Ave FC', 12), ('Clube Sport Marítimo', 10)]\nValue samples: ['€0', '€1.1M', '€1.2M', '€1.3M', '€1.4M'] ['€950K', '€975K', '€9M']\n","metadata":{"output":"Brasileirao seasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014'] ... ['2020', '2021', '2022']\nCup seasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014'] ... ['2019', '2020', '2021']\nLib seasons: ['2013', '2014', '2015'] ... ['2021', '2022', 'NA']\nNovo years: ['2003', '2004', '2005'] ... ['2017', '2018', '2019']\nBR years: ['2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022', '2023']\n\nFIFA rows: 18207\nBrazilian players by club (top 20): [('Grêmio', 20), ('Atlético Mineiro', 20), ('Cruzeiro', 20), ('Fluminense', 20), ('Santos', 20), ('Internacional', 20), ('América FC (Minas Gerais)', 20), ('Botafogo', 20), ('Bahia', 20), ('Paraná', 20), ('Atlético Paranaense', 20), ('Vitória', 20), ('Sport Club do Recife', 20), ('Chapecoense', 20), ('Ceará Sporting Club', 20), ('Portimonense SC', 18), ('SC Braga', 13), ('CD Aves', 12), ('Rio Ave FC', 12), ('Clube Sport Marítimo', 10)]\nValue samples: ['€0', '€1.1M', '€1.2M', '€1.3M', '€1.4M'] ['€950K', '€975K', '€9M']\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\n\n# Seasons per file\ndef seasons(path, col, enc='utf-8'):\n    with open(path, newline='', encoding=enc) as f:\n        vals = Counter(r[col].strip() for r in csv.DictReader(f) if r.get(col))\n    return sorted(vals)\n\nprint(\"Brasileirao seasons:\", seasons('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv','season')[:3], \"...\", seasons('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv','season')[-3:])\nprint(\"Cup seasons:\", seasons('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv','season')[:3], \"...\", seasons('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv','season')[-3:])\nprint(\"Lib seasons:\", seasons('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv','season')[:3], \"...\", seasons('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv','season')[-3:])\nprint(\"Novo years:\", seasons('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv','Ano')[:3], \"...\", seasons('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv','Ano')[-3:])\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    years = Counter(r['date'][:4] for r in csv.DictReader(f) if r.get('date'))\nprint(\"BR years:\", sorted(years))\n\n# FIFA clubs w/ Brazil\nwith open('data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    clubs = Counter(); nats = Counter(); vals=set()\n    rows=0\n    for row in r:\n        rows+=1\n        if row['Nationality']=='Brazil': clubs[row['Club']]+=1\n        vals.add(row['Value'])\nprint(\"\\nFIFA rows:\", rows)\nprint(\"Brazilian players by club (top 20):\", clubs.most_common(20))\nprint(\"Value samples:\", sorted(vals)[:5], sorted(vals)[-3:])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788226636769,"end":1788226636772}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I have a good picture of team name variations. Key normalization approach:\n\n1. **Strip state/country suffixes**: \"-SP\", \"-RJ\" (state abbreviations), \" (URU)\", \"-PAR\", \"-EQU\" (country codes), \" - MG\" (with spaces like in Cup file \"América - MG\").\n2. **Alias map** for canonicalization of major teams:\n   - \"Atletico-MG\"/\"Atlético-MG\"/\"Atlético Mineiro\"/\"Atletico Mineiro\" → \"Atlético Mineiro\"\n   - \"Athletico-PR\"/\"Atlético-PR\"/\"Athletico Paranaense\"/\"Atletico Paranaense\" → \"Athletico Paranaense\"\n   - \"Atlético-GO\"/\"Atletico-GO\"/\"Atletico Goianiense\" → \"Atlético Goianiense\"\n   - \"América-MG\"/\"America MG\" → \"América Mineiro\"\n   - \"América-RN\"/\"America RN\" → \"América de Natal\"\n   - \"Vasco\"/\"Vasco da Gama\" → \"Vasco da Gama\"\n   - \"Sao Paulo\"/\"São Paulo\" → \"São Paulo\"\n   - \"Gremio\" → \"Grêmio\", \"Avai\" → \"Avaí\", \"Csa\"/\"CSA\" → \"CSA\"\n   - \"Atletico\"/\"Athletico\" (Libertadores) → \"Athletico Paranaense\"\n   - \"Cuiaba\" → \"Cuiabá\", \"Ceara\" → \"Ceará\", \"Nautico\" → \"Náutico\", \"Vitoria\" → \"Vitória\", \"Goias\" → \"Goiás\", \"Criciuma\" → \"Criciúma\"\n   \n   Strategy: normalize to a canonical display name via alias dict; unmatched names get a generic normalization: strip suffix, title-case-ish with accents preserved where possible.\n\nFor robust matching (fuzzy), also keep an index of accent-stripped lowercase names.\n\n3. **Date parsing**: formats: \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\", \"%Y-%m-%d\", \"%d/%m/%Y\", plus date might be empty.\n\nNow, the design:\n\n**Files:**\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/__init__.py`\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py` — team name + date normalization\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py` — loads all 6 CSVs into unified `Match` and `Player` dataclasses\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py` — query engine\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/server.py` — MCP server exposing tools\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/__main__.py`\n- `tests/` — pytest tests, including BDD-style\n- `requirements.txt`\n\nLet me now think carefully about what the unified Match record should be, and the queries:\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass Match:\n    date: str | None          # ISO \"YYYY-MM-DD\"\n    season: int | None\n    competition: str          # canonical: \"Brasileirão\", \"Copa do Brasil\", \"Libertadores\", \"Serie A\"/\"Serie B\"/\"Serie C\" (from BR dataset)\n    round: str | None\n    stage: str | None\n    home_team: str            # canonical display name\n    away_team: str\n    home_goals: int | None\n    away_goals: int | None\n    home_state: str | None\n    away_state: str | None\n    arena: str | None\n    source: str               # file name\n```\n\nNote: BR-Football-Dataset has tournaments \"Serie A\", \"Serie B\", \"Serie C\", \"Copa do Brasil\". For competition queries, spec mentions Brasileirão, Copa do Brasil, Libertadores. I'll keep \"Serie A\"/\"Serie B\"/\"Serie C\" as-is but also treat \"Serie A\" as a Brasileirão-equivalent in competition matching (competition filter with alias matching: \"brasileirao\" → {\"Brasileirão\", \"Serie A\", \"Serie B\"?}). Hmm, careful: \"Serie B\" is not Brasileirão. Competition filter: normalize competition name: \"brasileirão\"/\"brasileirao\"/\"serie a\"/\"brasileirao serie a\" → matches \"Brasileirão\" (from Brasileirao_Matches.csv) and \"Serie A\" (from BR dataset). That gives better coverage for standings across years (e.g. 2019 Brasileirão from BR dataset Serie A 2019 + Brasileirao_Matches 2019).\n\nActually wait — potential duplicates: Brasileirao_Matches.csv covers 2012-2023(?) and novo_campeonato covers 2003-2019, and BR dataset Serie A covers some years too. Duplicates across files for the same match are possible (e.g. 2012-2019 overlap between Brasileirao_Matches and novo_campeonato, and BR Serie A). For standings, duplicates would corrupt results. I need dedup: same competition (league), same date, same teams (home/away) → treat as the same match. I'll implement dedup on (competition_class, date, home, away) where competition_class groups \"Brasileirão\" and \"Serie A\" as \"league\". Hmm, but they could genuinely be different tournaments on the same date with same teams (unlikely for league). Dedup key: (league_class, date, home_canonical, away_canonical). For cup/Libertadores, dates+teams+stage could repeat (two legs have different dates so fine).\n\nWhich source wins on dedup? Preference order: prefer the one with more info... Let me just keep the first by a priority: novo_campeonato has arena + state; Brasileirao_Matches has state + round. I'll dedup by key and prefer records from files in a priority order: [\"novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\", \"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\", \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\"] for league-class. Actually simpler: dedup after loading, keep first occurrence with priority list. Let me check the date overlap: novo covers 2003-2019, Brasileirao_Matches 2012-2024?, BR Serie A 2012?-2023?\n\nLet me check seasons in each file.\n\nFor standings computation, use league matches only (competition class \"league\"), for a given season, computed from home/away results: 3 pts win, 1 draw. Sort by points, then wins, then goal diff, then goals for. Champion = first. Relegation: last 4 (for 20-team seasons) — but rather than hardcoding, I can mark bottom 4 as \"relegation zone\" only if 20 teams. Hmm, keep it simple: return standings; mark top as Champion. For relegation question \"Which teams were relegated in 2020?\" — bottom 4 of 20-team table. I'll include a note when table has 20 teams.\n\nPlayer queries: fifa_data.csv columns: ID, Name, Age, Photo, Nationality, Flag, Overall, Potential, Club, Club Logo, Value, Wage, Special, Preferred Foot, ..., Position, Jersey Number, Joined, Loaned From, Contract Valid Until, Height, Weight, ... skill ratings. I'll extract a subset: ID, Name, Age, Nationality, Overall, Potential, Club, Position, Jersey Number, Height, Weight, Value, Wage, plus a few skill ratings (Finishing, Dribbling, Passing? there's no \"Passing\" — there's ShortPassing; also Crossing, Finishing, Dribbling, BallControl, SprintSpeed, ShotPower...). I'll keep a generic subset: Crossing, Finishing, Dribbling, ShortPassing, BallControl, SprintSpeed, ShotPower, Strength, GKDiving? Keep it moderate: name, age, nationality, overall, potential, club, position, jersey number, height, weight, value, wage, preferred foot + top skills. Maybe I include a dict of all numeric skill columns that are non-null? That could bloat. I'll include a curated list.\n\nCross-file queries: e.g., \"players at Flamengo\" + Flamengo matches. I'll add a tool `get_club_overview(team)` that combines: team stats from matches + players at that club (fuzzy club match). That satisfies \"Cross-file queries work (e.g., player + match data)\".\n\nClub name matching in FIFA data: Brazilian clubs in FIFA dataset — let me check what clubs look like (e.g. \"Flamengo\"?). Let me check.\n\nAlso derbies: \"Show me all derbies in 2023\" — need a list of traditional rivalries. I'll add a small derby map: Fla-Flu (Flamengo vs Fluminense), Clássico dos Milhões (Flamengo vs Vasco), Choque-Rei (Palmeiras vs São Paulo), Majestoso (Corinthians vs São Paulo), Dérbi Paulista (Corinthians vs Palmeiras), Clássico dos Milhões, Gre-Nal (Grêmio vs Internacional), Ba-Vi (Bahia vs Vitória), Clássico dos Gigantes?, Atletiba (Athletico vs Coritiba), Tie-Co (?), Clássico Reinaldo? I'll include major ones and a tool `search_matches(..., derby_only=True)` or `list_derbies(season=...)`. Simpler: derby detection function is_derby(home, away) checks pair sets. Add tool `search_derbies(season=None, competition=None)`.\n\nSample questions to cover (≥20) in tests:\n1. Show me all Flamengo vs Fluminense matches → search_matches(\"Flamengo\", \"Fluminense\")\n2. What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023? → search_matches(team=\"Palmeiras\", season=2023)\n3. Find all Copa do Brasil finals → search_matches(competition=\"Copa do Brasil\", round contains \"final\")\n4. Corinthians home record 2022 → get_team_stats(\"Corinthians\", season=2022, venue=\"home\")\n5. Which team scored the most goals in Serie A 2023 → get_standings/compute\n6. Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head → head_to_head\n7. Find all Brazilian players → search_players(nationality=\"Brazil\")\n8. Highest-rated players at Flamengo → search_players(club=\"Flamengo\", sort overall)\n9. Forwards from São Paulo FC → search_players(club=\"São Paulo\", position=\"ST/LW/CF\"...) — position filter: match prefix? FIFA positions: ST, CF, LW, RW, etc. \"forwards\" → positions in {ST, CF, LW, RW, LS, RS, LF, RF}. I'll support position_category=\"forward|midfielder|defender|goalkeeper\".\n10. Who won the 2019 Brasileirão → get_standings(\"Brasileirão\", 2019)[0]\n11. Which teams were relegated in 2020 → standings bottom\n12. Average goals per match in Brasileirão → get_competition_stats\n13. Which team has best away record → aggregate\n14. Biggest wins → get_competition_stats / top margin\n15. When did Flamengo last play Corinthians → head_to_head last meeting\n16. Who is Gabriel Barbosa → search_players(name=\"Gabriel Barbosa\")\n17. Which players play for Flamengo → search_players(club=\"Flamengo\")\n18. Show me all derbies in 2023 → search_derbies(season=2023)\n19. What competitions has Palmeiras played in → get_team_competitions(\"Palmeiras\")\n20. Compare 2018 and 2019 seasons → season summary tool get_season_summary(season)\n21. What was the score? — last match between teams returns scores.\n\nOK. Tools for the MCP server (these become MCP tools):\n1. `search_matches(team, opponent, competition, season, date_from, date_to, stage_or_round, limit)` \n2. `get_team_stats(team, competition, season, venue)`\n3. `head_to_head(team_a, team_b)`\n4. `search_players(name, nationality, club, position, position_category, min_overall, max_overall, limit)` + sort\n5. `get_standings(competition, season)`\n6. `get_competition_stats(competition, season)` (avg goals, home win rate, biggest wins, top scoring teams)\n7. `search_derbies(season, competition)` \n8. `get_team_competitions(team)`\n9. `get_season_summary(season)` / `compare_seasons(season_a, season_b)`\n10. `get_club_overview(team)` — cross-file: matches summary + players\n11. `list_teams(competition)` maybe helpful for discovery\n12. `list_competitions()` / `list_seasons(competition)`\n\nThat's a good set. Keep tools focused (MCP best practice: fewer, well-described tools). Maybe consolidate: list_competitions + list_teams into `list_entities`? No — keep list_teams and drop list_competitions? I'll keep both small ones; fine.\n\nNow performance: loading 10k+18k rows with csv module is fine (<2s). Build in-memory indexes at startup.\n\nLet me check FIFA club names and Brazilian nationality, plus seasons per file, and check BR dataset date/season coverage. Also confirm Libertadores goal columns are strings (\"2\").","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05a9d0afc001XZyDsFuH8v0BHo","sessionID":"ses_fa566fb65ffeJ8k4Q5FXGIEPJE","messageID":"msg_05a9baa2e001m5CI8GY2pSuWQi"}}
