{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788226675082,"sessionID":"ses_fa566fb65ffeJ8k4Q5FXGIEPJE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_2c56f22494c8407695d6adde","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    print(\"Cup rounds:\", sorted(set(r['round'] for r in csv.DictReader(f)), key=lambda x:(len(x),x)))\nwith open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    print(\"Lib stages:\", sorted(set(r['stage'] for r in csv.DictReader(f))))\n# empty goals check\nfor path, cols in [('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv',['home_goal','away_goal']),\n                   ('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv',['home_goal','away_goal']),\n                   ('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv',['Gols_mandante','Gols_visitante'])]:\n    with open(path, newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        vals={c: Counter() for c in cols}\n        for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for c in cols:\n                v=(r.get(c) or '').strip()\n                if not v or v.lower()=='na': vals[c]['_empty']+=1\n    print(path, dict(vals))\nEOF"},"output":"Cup rounds: ['1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6', '7', '8']\nLib stages: ['final', 'group stage', 'quarterfinals', 'round of 16', 'semifinals']\ndata/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv {'home_goal': Counter({'_empty': 82}), 'away_goal': Counter({'_empty': 82})}\ndata/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv {'home_goal': Counter(), 'away_goal': Counter()}\ndata/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv {'Gols_mandante': Counter(), 'Gols_visitante': Counter()}\n","metadata":{"output":"Cup rounds: ['1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6', '7', '8']\nLib stages: ['final', 'group stage', 'quarterfinals', 'round of 16', 'semifinals']\ndata/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv {'home_goal': Counter({'_empty': 82}), 'away_goal': Counter({'_empty': 82})}\ndata/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv {'home_goal': Counter(), 'away_goal': Counter()}\ndata/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv {'Gols_mandante': Counter(), 'Gols_visitante': Counter()}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    print(\"Cup rounds:\", sorted(set(r['round'] for r in csv.DictReader(f)), key=lambda x:(len(x),x)))\nwith open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    print(\"Lib stages:\", sorted(set(r['stage'] for r in csv.DictReader(f))))\n# empty goals check\nfor path, cols in [('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv',['home_goal','away_goal']),\n                   ('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv',['home_goal','away_goal']),\n                   ('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv',['Gols_mandante','Gols_visitante'])]:\n    with open(path, newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        vals={c: Counter() for c in cols}\n        for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for c in cols:\n                v=(r.get(c) or '').strip()\n                if not v or v.lower()=='na': vals[c]['_empty']+=1\n    print(path, dict(vals))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788226675078,"end":1788226675081}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"FIFA data does NOT have Flamengo, Palmeiras, São Paulo, Corinthians clubs. Interesting — it's a FIFA 19 dataset with limited clubs (probably top clubs only, ~20 per league for major leagues). So example questions like \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\" won't return results, but the tool must handle it gracefully (return empty + note). \"São Paulo FC\" → no club. There are clubs \"Santos\", \"Bahia\", \"Botafogo\", \"Cruzeiro\", \"Fluminense\", \"Grêmio\", \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\".\n\nClub matching: fuzzy contains-based, e.g., club=\"Santos\" would also match \"Santos Laguna\" — need exact-match preference and rank matches: exact > starts_with > contains. Return matched club info in the response so it's transparent.\n\nNationality \"Brazil\" for Brazilians.\n\nNow, date handling in BR dataset: date \"2023-09-24\", fine.\n\nNow — Libertadores goals are strings like \"2\"; handle via safe int parse (and \"NA\" → None). Also Libertadores has \"NA\" seasons.\n\nCup rounds: values like \"1\", \"2\", ..., \"final\"? Let me check round values in Cup and Libertadores stage values quickly. Also check novo_campeonato \"OBS\" column and whether datetime in Brasileirao has empty values.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05a9da131001FsBP5jppahXm6e","sessionID":"ses_fa566fb65ffeJ8k4Q5FXGIEPJE","messageID":"msg_05a9d4cfc001Oi1yN5s4J9cc4i"}}
