final\" for Libertadores; for the cup I could map the max round per season as \"final\"? That's risky. Better: `search_matches` supports `stage`/`round` filter with substring matching, and I'll compute cup finals as the last round of each season only if asked... Keep it honest: expose round filter. For \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\" test, I'll use Libertadores for stage=\"final\" and for cup use round filter; but the spec example says \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\". I could add logic: for cup competitions, label matches where round == max round of that season as \"Final\". Hmm — actually in the Copa do Brasil, ties are two-legged; the final would be 2 matches with the highest round number. Number of rounds varies by season (8 in 2012? in 2013+ format changed to fewer rounds with playoffs). Let me check rounds per season... Not worth deep-diving; a generic \"finals\" detection: for cup competitions, group by season, matches whose round equals the max numeric round for that season are finals. For two-legged ties that yields 2 matches per final, which is correct! Let me verify rounds per season count to make sure max round is final-ish.\n\n- Brasileirao_Matches has 82 matches with empty goals (probably future/suspended matches — 2020 COVID?). Those should be kept but excluded from standings/stats (goals None).\n\nLet me quickly check cup rounds per season to confirm max-round = final assumption.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05a9dfc610011vHYmEJ5svqLqP","sessionID":"ses_fa566fb65ffeJ8k4Q5FXGIEPJE","messageID":"msg_05a9da2e3001Yl1DLWDWtpVJdu"}}
