{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788227090576,"sessionID":"ses_fa566fb65ffeJ8k4Q5FXGIEPJE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_5db47654903d4171961eec7e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-75154ofp/retort-0076cc65ba78/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","oldString":"    \"abc\": \"ABC\",\n    \"abc rn\": \"ABC\",\n    \"as a\": \"ASA\",\n    \"aguia negra\": \"Águia Negra\",\n    \"aimore\": \"Aimoré\",","newString":"    \"abc\": \"ABC\",\n    \"abc rn\": \"ABC\",\n    \"a s a\": \"ASA\",\n    \"a s a al\": \"ASA\",\n    \"asa al\": \"ASA\",\n    \"aguia negra\": \"Águia Negra\",\n    \"aimore\": \"Aimoré\","},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-75154ofp/retort-0076cc65ba78/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-75154ofp/retort-0076cc65ba78/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-75154ofp/retort-0076cc65ba78/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -104,9 +104,11 @@\n \"chapecoense\": \"Chapecoense\",\n \"atletico de capelense\": \"Atlético Capelense\",\n \"abc\": \"ABC\",\n \"abc rn\": \"ABC\",\n-\"as a\": \"ASA\",\n+\"a s a\": \"ASA\",\n+\"a s a al\": \"ASA\",\n+\"asa al\": \"ASA\",\n \"aguia negra\": \"Águia Negra\",\n \"aimore\": \"Aimoré\",\n \"avai\": \"Avaí\",\n \"ceara\": \"Ceará\",\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-75154ofp/retort-0076cc65ba78/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-75154ofp/retort-0076cc65ba78/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-75154ofp/retort-0076cc65ba78/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-75154ofp/retort-0076cc65ba78/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -104,9 +104,11 @@\n \"chapecoense\": \"Chapecoense\",\n \"atletico de capelense\": \"Atlético Capelense\",\n \"abc\": \"ABC\",\n \"abc rn\": \"ABC\",\n-\"as a\": \"ASA\",\n+\"a s a\": \"ASA\",\n+\"a s a al\": \"ASA\",\n+\"asa al\": \"ASA\",\n \"aguia negra\": \"Águia Negra\",\n \"aimore\": \"Aimoré\",\n \"avai\": \"Avaí\",\n \"ceara\": \"Ceará\",\n","additions":3,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788227090572,"end":1788227090574}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"This confirms the danger. Space-suffixed names in BR dataset are legion, and several collide with real clubs:\n- \"Botafogo RJ\" → Botafogo ✓, but \"Botafogo PB\" (João Pessoa) and \"Botafogo SP\" (Ribeirão Preto) are DIFFERENT clubs that must NOT become \"Botafogo\".\n- \"Fluminense RJ\" ✓ vs \"Fluminense PI\" (Fluminense de Feira is BA... actually \"Fluminense PI\" = Fluminense do Piauí? hmm) — different club.\n- \"Santos AP\" (Santos-AP) vs \"Santos\" (SP) — different!\n- \"Santa Cruz RN\" vs \"Santa Cruz RS\" vs \"Santa Cruz\" (PE) — different!\n- \"Vitoria ES\" vs \"Vitória\" (BA) — different!\n- \"Nautico RR\" vs \"Náutico\" (PE) — different!\n- \"Guarani SP\" vs \"Guarani\" (SP) — same actually (Guarani is from Campinas SP) ✓.\n- \"Coritiba PR\", \"Cuiaba MT\", \"Caxias RS\", \"Internacional RS\", \"Gremio RS\", \"Juventude MA\" (vs Juventude RS! — \"Juventude MA\" is Juventude de São Luís? hmm MA state — different club), \"Botafogo RJ\"...\n\nGiven the prevalence and ambiguity, space-separated suffix stripping is too dangerous for the BR dataset. Decision: only strip suffixes with an explicit separator \"-\" / \"–\" / \"(\" — NOT a bare space. But then \"America MG\" (BR) won't hit alias \"america mg\" via suffix path... but full-key alias lookup happens FIRST: \"america mg\" is in the alias table → resolves to \"América Mineiro\" ✓ without stripping. So space-suffixed variants that need disambiguation go through explicit alias entries; the rest stay as distinct display names (fine).\n\nSo I need to add explicit full-key aliases for the colliding/major BR space-suffixed names so cross-file consistency works:\n- \"botafogo pb\" → \"Botafogo-PB\"\n- \"botafogo sp\" → \"Botafogo-SP\"\n- \"botafogo rj\" → \"Botafogo\"\n- \"fluminense rj\" → \"Fluminense\"  (novo uses \"Fluminense\"; Brasileirao file \"Fluminense-RJ\" strips → \"Fluminense\" ✓)\n- \"fluminense pi\" → \"Fluminense-PI\"\n- \"santos ap\" → \"Santos-AP\"\n- \"santa cruz rn\" → \"Santa Cruz-RN\"\n- \"santa cruz rs\" → \"Santa Cruz-RS\"\n- \"santa cruz\" → \"Santa Cruz\" (PE, canonical — alias identity)\n- \"vitoria es\" → \"Vitória-ES\"\n- \"nautico rr\" → \"Náutico-RR\"\n- \"juventude ma\" → \"Juventude-MA\"  (distinct from Juventude RS)\n- \"america rn\" ✓ have\n- \"americano rj\" → \"Americano-RJ\"? display \"Americano\" is fine but keep distinct: \"Americano-RJ\"\n- \"boavista rj\" ✓ have → \"Boavista\"\n- \"cuiaba mt\" → \"Cuiabá\"\n- \"coritiba pr\" → \"Coritiba\"\n- \"gremio rs\" → \"Grêmio\"\n- \"internacional rs\" → \"Internacional\"\n- \"caxias rs\" → \"Caxias\"\n- \"guarani sp\" → \"Guarani\"\n- \"audax sp\" → \"Audax-SP\"? Brasileirao file has \"Audax-SP\"? No — Brasileirao file doesn't have Audax. Cup has \"Audax - SP\" → strip → \"Audax\" → so alias \"audax sp\" → \"Audax\" for consistency. OK.\n- \"vasco da gama rj\" → \"Vasco da Gama\" (BR has \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\")\n- \"nacional am\" → \"Nacional-AM\" (distinct from Uruguayan Nacional! Both map... hmm, alias \"nacional\" → \"Nacional\" and \"nacional uru\" → \"Nacional\" — collision with Nacional-AM. Libertadores Nacional = URU. BR Serie C had Nacional-AM. Rarely queried together; but to be safe: \"nacional am\" → \"Nacional-AM\". The Uruguayan one stays \"Nacional\". OK.)\n- \"athletic club mg\" → \"Athletic Club\" (BR) — distinct from Athletico Paranaense; no strip needed (ends \"MG\" state → full key not aliased → display fallback \"Athletic Club MG\"? Without space-stripping it stays \"Athletic Club MG\" — fine, distinct name.)\n- \"operario pr\"/\"operario ms\"/\"operario mt\" — distinct clubs; leave as-is (no aliases).\n- \"sao jose rs\"/\"sao jose pa\"? \"Sao Jose PA\" — PA = Pará? Hmm \"São José-RS\" and \"São José-PA\". Leave as-is.\n- \"sao raimundo am/pa/rr\" leave as-is.\n- \"rio branco ac/es\" leave as-is.\n- \"ypiranga ap/rs\" leave.\n- \"bragantino pa\" → \"Bragantino-PA\" (Clube do Remo? no, \"Bragantino-PA\" is a Pará club) — MUST not alias to Red Bull Bragantino! My alias \"bragantino\" → \"Red Bull Bragantino\" — careful: only bare \"bragantino\" (no suffix) maps. \"Bragantino PA\" full key \"bragantino pa\" → needs alias → \"Bragantino-PA\" to prevent... wait, without space-stripping, \"Bragantino PA\" never becomes \"bragantino\" anyway. But should I keep bare \"bragantino\" → \"Red Bull Bragantino\"? The cup file might have \"Bragantino - SP\" (hyphen!) → strip → \"Bragantino\" → alias → Red Bull Bragantino ✓ good (Cup 2012? Bragantino played Copa do Brasil). OK keep, and add \"bragantino pa\" → \"Bragantino-PA\".\n\nBut also hyphen-suffixed in BR: \"Aguia Negra-MS\" (strip ✓), \"Guarani-SP\" (strip → \"Guarani\" ✓ alias).\n\nNow, about the \"space\" suffix issue in the CUP file: names there use \" - \" separator like \"América - MG\" — hyphen present ✓ strips fine. Brasileirao file uses \"-\" no space ✓. So space-only stripping is never needed. \n\nAlso \"4 de Julho EC\" etc fine.\n\nOne more: \"Sao Raimundo RR\" etc — display keeps \"Sao\" without accent... display fallback not applied (no strip) so original \"Sao Raimundo RR\" preserved as-is — fine.\n\nAlso, for the \"no strip\" path I return `cleaned` (original casing). Good — preserves \"Nacional (URU)\"? No wait — \"Nacional (URU)\" full key \"nacional uru\" → alias ✓. But e.g. \"Alianza Lima\" stays.\n\nEdge in normalize_team: what if name has BOTH weird spacing like \"Atlético  -  PR\"? collapse_ws handles.\n\nAlso: hyphenated club names that aren't suffixes: \"Rio Branco-AC\"? only if ends with state code. \"Ypiranga-AP\"? Not in data probably. \"Nacional-URU\" style handled. What about real names ending in \"-XX\" that are NOT state codes: \"Peñarol-MVD\"? not in data. Fine.\n\nBut wait — one real problem: hyphen-strip on \"Gremio-RS\" → \"Gremio\" → alias → \"Grêmio\" ✓. And \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" ✓.\n\nAnother: \"Red Bull Bragantino-SP\" → strip → \"Red Bull Bragantino\" → alias ✓.\n\nNow update the regex: separator pattern `[-–]` or `(` — i.e. `[-–(]+` but NOT bare space (already true — space isn't in the class; the separator must be one of those chars). My current regex already requires `[-–(]+` — space alone does NOT match since the class excludes space. \"America MG\": regex `^(.+?)\\s*[-–(]+\\s*([A-Za-z]{2,3})\\s*\\)?$` — needs a `[-–(]` char before code; \"America MG\" has none → no match → no strip ✓. \n\nSo the regex is already safe. I just need to add the extra full-key aliases for cross-file consistency of space-suffixed variants. Let me now rewrite the alias additions and remove the silly \"brazil\" entry, fix \"as a\" key.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05aa3f879001mBAeJ6CmGgtfLx","sessionID":"ses_fa566fb65ffeJ8k4Q5FXGIEPJE","messageID":"msg_05aa3042c001AoRbAP0NVHlDsC"}}
