({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 38, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 19})\nhome: 28\n\nGabriel names: ['D. Gabriele', 'Gabriel', 'Gabriel Boschilia', 'Gabriel Jesus', 'Gabriel Nunes', 'Gabriel Paulista', 'Gabriel Silva', 'Gabriel Xavier', 'Gabrielzinho', 'João Gabriel', 'R. Gabrielsen', 'R. Pierre-Gabriel']\n","metadata":{"output":"Flamengo 2019 total in merged: 50\nby source: Counter({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 38, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 12})\ndup dates: [('2019-06-01', 2), ('2019-08-04', 2), ('2019-08-10', 2), ('2019-11-10', 2), ('2019-11-17', 2)]\n -> 2019-06-01 Flamengo 2 0 Fortaleza FC BR-Football-Dataset.csv\n -> 2019-06-01 Flamengo 2 0 Fortaleza Brasileirao_Matches.csv\n\nCorinthians 2022: 57 Counter({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 38, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 19})\nhome: 28\n\nGabriel names: ['D. Gabriele', 'Gabriel', 'Gabriel Boschilia', 'Gabriel Jesus', 'Gabriel Nunes', 'Gabriel Paulista', 'Gabriel Silva', 'Gabriel Xavier', 'Gabrielzinho', 'João Gabriel', 'R. Gabrielsen', 'R. Pierre-Gabriel']\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.data_loader import Dataset, _read_csv\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.normalize import normalize_team\nfrom collections import Counter\nds = Dataset()\n\n# 1. Flamengo 2019 matches by source\nfla = [m for m in ds.matches if m.competition==\"Brasileirão\" and m.season==2019 and \"Flamengo\" in (m.home_team, m.away_team)]\nprint(\"Flamengo 2019 total in merged:\", len(fla))\nprint(\"by source:\", Counter(m.source for m in fla))\ndates = Counter(m.date for m in fla)\ndups = {d:c for d,c in dates.items() if c>1}\nprint(\"dup dates:\", list(dups.items())[:5])\n\n# compare raw rows for a dup date\nsample = sorted(dups)[0]\nfor m in fla:\n    if m.date==sample:\n        print(\" ->\", m.date, m.home_team, m.home_goals, m.away_goals, m.away_team, m.source)\n\n# 2. Corinthians home 2022\ncor = [m for m in ds.matches if m.competition==\"Brasileirão\" and m.season==2022 and \"Corinthians\" in (m.home_team, m.away_team)]\nprint(\"\\nCorinthians 2022:\", len(cor), Counter(m.source for m in cor))\nhome = [m for m in cor if m.home_team==\"Corinthians\"]\nprint(\"home:\", len(home))\n\n# 3. FIFA Gabriel\nimport csv\nwith open('data/kaggle/fifa_data.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    hits = [r['Name'] for r in csv.DictReader(f) if 'gabriel' in r['Name'].lower()]\nprint(\"\\nGabriel names:\", sorted(set(hits))[:20])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788227546710,"end":1788227546727}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Several problems to fix:\n\n1. **Load time 0.82s** — fine (<2s).\n\n2. **Brasileirão count 9882** — 4180 (Brasileirao) + 6886 (novo) = 11066, minus dedup, plus BR Serie A (~2400?). Let me sanity-check dedup. 9882 seems plausible-ish but standings show problems:\n\n3. **2019 standings WRONG**: Flamengo 121 points?! A 38-game season max is 114. And complete=False. So duplicate matches are NOT being deduped properly. Why? Because my dedup key requires `match.date` to be set AND equal across sources. Sources: Brasileirao_Matches 2019 has dates like \"2019-12-05 21:00:00\" → date \"2019-12-05\". BR Serie A has date \"2019-12-05\"? Also datetime might differ in time but I store date only ✓. novo has 2019 too (\"DD/MM/YYYY\"). Hmm — so why 121 points for Flamengo?\n\nWait: 121 points means ~40 games with 40 wins? No — Flamengo 2019: 28W. 121/3 = 40 wins +1? That means many duplicate matches counted. Possibly the dedup key failed because of **team name normalization differences between sources** — e.g., Brasileirao \"Flamengo-RJ\" → \"Flamengo\" vs BR \"Flamengo\" → \"Flamengo\" ✓ same. Dates? Let me debug: check counts for (Flamengo, 2019) matches in Brasileirão competition.\n\nActually, likely cause: BR \"Serie A\" matches for 2019 have different dates from Brasileirao_Matches! The BR dataset might store a different date (e.g., rescheduled?) or a date format issue... or the BR Serie A dataset might cover only *som